rl":"https://stablecoins.llama.fi/stablecoinchains","methodology_note":"Stablecoin circulating supply and DeFi TVL are different DefiLlama measures and must not be added together."},"team":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","founders":[{"name":"Nikolai Durov","role":"original TON architect","prior":"Telegram technical co-founder","source_url":"https://ton.org/primer.pdf"},{"name":"Pavel Durov","role":"Telegram founder and original TON sponsor","prior":"Telegram","source_url":"https://ton.org/primer.pdf"},{"name":"Anatoliy Makosov","role":"Newton open-source community initiator","prior":null,"source_url":"https://ton.org/primer.pdf"},{"name":"EmelyanenkoK","role":"Newton open-source community initiator","prior":null,"source_url":"https://ton.org/primer.pdf"}],"entity":"TON Foundation and open-source validator community; Telegram''s original project and the present Foundation are distinct.","key_events":[{"date":"2020-06-26","type":"regulatory","description":"A court-approved SEC settlement required Telegram to return more than $1.2B and pay an $18.5M penalty for the original Gram offering.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2020-146"},{"date":"2021-05","type":"rebrand","description":"Newton became TON Foundation as Testnet2 became Mainnet.","source_url":"https://ton.org/primer.pdf"},{"date":"2026-06-01","type":"rebrand","description":"The official native currency name changed from Toncoin to Gram.","source_url":"https://ton.org/en"}],"regulatory_status":"The SEC settlement concerned Telegram Group and TON Issuer''s original offering. It must not be represented as an adjudication that today''s community-distributed GRAM itself is a security."},"narrative":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","purpose":"A custom asynchronous, dynamically sharded L1 for Telegram-native mini apps, payments, digital assets, and consumer services.","positioning":"TON uses Telegram distribution and a custom TVM/actor architecture to pursue consumer-scale payments, mini apps, collectibles, identities, and services.","competitors":[{"name":"Tron","relationship":"stablecoin transfer and payment competitor"},{"name":"Solana","relationship":"consumer application and payments competitor"},{"name":"Plasma","relationship":"stablecoin-specialized consumer payment competitor"}],"narrative_arc":"The chain survived Telegram''s regulatory withdrawal through an open-source continuation, later gained Telegram-native distribution, and renamed its asset back to Gram in 2026.","media_sentiment":"mixed"},"risk":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","exploits":[],"sanctions":{"flagged":false,"detail":"No chain-level designation is asserted by this dossier; an archived exact-name SDN review remains an explicit publication gap."},"extraction_flags":["platform_dependency","custom_vm_risk","regulatory_legacy","defi_contraction"],"audit_status":null,"risks":[{"type":"platform_dependency","detail":"The consumer thesis depends heavily on continued Telegram integration and distribution.","source_url":"https://ton.org/en"},{"type":"regulatory_legacy","detail":"Telegram''s original Gram offering ended in an SEC settlement, creating persistent lifecycle confusion even though the current community network is distinct.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2020-146"},{"type":"liveness_and_capacity","detail":"The December 2023 inscription surge exposed validator-performance and shard-split bottlenecks under load.","source_url":"https://ton.org/en/technical-report-december-5-inscriptions-launch-on-ton"},{"type":"defi_contraction","detail":"Current DeFi TVL is 92% below its 2024 peak despite much larger stablecoin circulation.","source_url":"https://api.llama.fi/v2/historicalChainTvl/TON"}]},"synthesis":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","situation":"TON records only $62.1M DeFi TVL, 92% below peak, yet about $790M in stablecoins and $27.66M in 30-day fees; its usage thesis is Telegram payments and mini apps rather than DeFi TVL alone.","postmortem":null,"why":"TON persists because the open-source community preserved the original architecture after Telegram withdrew, then gained a distribution advantage through Telegram-native wallets, mini apps, payments, and digital assets.","success_mechanism":"Telegram distribution, low-cost custom execution, asynchronous sharding, and native consumer primitives can reach users who never interact with a conventional DeFi front end.","strategic_choices":["Continue the original custom TVM and asynchronous-sharding architecture rather than adopt EVM.","Use Telegram as the dominant consumer and developer distribution channel.","Separate the community network from Telegram''s failed issuance while retaining the TON architecture.","Rename Toncoin back to Gram in 2026 despite substantial legacy ticker adoption."],"unknowns":["The composition of the unusually high fee total relative to DeFi TVL and DEX volume.","Current validator-stake concentration and the economic relationship among Telegram, TON Foundation, and ecosystem operators.","Whether the Gram rename improves clarity or fragments exchange, wallet, and historical datasets.","Whether stablecoin circulation produces durable DeFi depth or GRAM value capture."],"lessons_learned":["Chain, issuer, token-offering, and community-continuation lifecycles must remain separate.","Consumer distribution can sustain activity that DeFi TVL does not capture.","Custom architecture creates differentiation and tooling/liveness costs."],"could_differ":"EVM compatibility might have accelerated DeFi portability, but would have sacrificed the custom asynchronous architecture and native Telegram stack.","outlook":{"bull":"Telegram-native payments and mini apps convert stablecoin circulation into durable consumer activity.","base":"TON remains a consumer/payments specialist with strong distribution and weak conventional DeFi depth.","bear":"Telegram dependency, custom tooling, and weak DeFi economics constrain growth while the rename fragments adoption.","most_likely":"base"},"cause_tags":["teleg